          "en": "The Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court on the Question of Compulsory Demolition of Illegal Buildings, Structures and Facilities was adopted at the 1,572nd meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 25 March 2013, is hereby promulgated, and shall come into force on 3 April 2013.\n27 March 2013\nThe Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of Compulsory Demolition of Illegal Buildings,\nStructures and Facilities\nFa Shi No. 5 [2013]\n(Adopted at the 1,572nd meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 25 March 2013; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 27 March 2013; coming into force on 3 April 2013)\nThe Higher People's Court of Beijing Municipality:\nIn accordance with the spirit of the relevant provisions of the Administrative Compulsion Law and the Urban and Rural Planning Law, as regards the compulsory demolition of illegal buildings, structures and facilities that violate the Urban and Rural Planning Law, the law has already conferred on administrative organs the power of compulsory enforcement, and a people's court shall not accept an application for non-litigation administrative enforcement submitted by an administrative organ."
