        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court on Whether a Savings Contract Dispute Arising from the Disclosure of a Bank Savings Card Password Resulting in the Deposit Being Obtained by Another Person by Fraud Should Be Accepted as a Civil Case was adopted at the 1,358th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 4 July 2005, is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 1 August 2005.\n25 July 2005\nThe Supreme People's Court\nReply on Whether a Savings Contract Dispute Arising from the Disclosure of a Bank Savings Card Password\nResulting in the Deposit Being Obtained by Another Person by Fraud Should Be Accepted\nas a Civil Case\nFa Shi No. 7 [2005]\n(Adopted at the 1,358th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 4 July 2005; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 25 July 2005; coming into force on 1 August 2005)\nThe Higher People's Court of Sichuan Province:\nYour court's Request for Instructions on Whether a Dispute Arising from the Disclosure by a Depositor of a Bank Savings Card Password, Which Resulted in the Deposit Being Obtained by Another Person by Fraud, Should Be Accepted as a Civil Case has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nWhere, as a result of the disclosure of a bank savings card password, another person forges the bank savings card and obtains the depositor's bank deposit by fraud, and the depositor institutes civil litigation on the basis of the savings contract concluded between the depositor and the bank, the people's court shall accept the case in accordance with law.\nThis is our reply."
        },
