          "en": "The Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question Whether a Defendant May, in Intellectual Property Infringement Litigation,\non the Ground that the Plaintiff Has Abused Its Rights, Claim Compensation for Reasonable Expenses\nFa Shi No. 11 [2021]\n(Adopted at the 1,840th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 31 May 2021; coming into force on 3 June 2021)\nThe Higher People's Court of Shanghai Municipality:\nYour court's Request for Instructions on the Question Whether, in Intellectual Property Infringement Litigation, a Defendant May, on the Ground that the Plaintiff Has Abused Its Rights, Claim Compensation for Reasonable Expenses (Hu Gao Fa No. 215 [2021]) has been received. After study, the following reply is given:\nIn intellectual property infringement litigation, where the defendant submits evidence proving that the plaintiff's action constitutes an abuse of rights as prescribed by law which damages the defendant's lawful rights and interests, and requests the plaintiff in accordance with law to compensate the reasonable lawyers' fees, travel expenses, accommodation and meal expenses and other expenses paid by the defendant as a result of that litigation, the people's court shall uphold the request in accordance with law. The defendant may also institute a separate action requesting the plaintiff to compensate the aforementioned reasonable expenses."
